// Laguna XS.2 / M.1 / XS-2.1 (Poolside) — Model configuration
// Source: https://huggingface.co/poolside/Laguna-XS.2 (2026-04),
// https://huggingface.co/poolside/Laguna-M.1 (2026-06) and
// https://huggingface.co/poolside/Laguna-XS-2.1 (2026-06).
// Verified against each repo's chat_template.jinja and generation_config.json.
//
// Three 2026 Poolside coding checkpoints, one template knob set: model_type
// "laguna", context 262,144 (config.json), text-only, gc default
// default_chat_template_kwargs {"enable_thinking": true}.
//
// WHY A SEPARATE FILE FROM Laguna-S-2.1: the S-2.1 preset sends
// preserve_thinking: true, and NONE of these three templates declare that
// variable (checked in every chat_template.jinja). Sending it here would be a
// knob the template ignores. Longest-match routing is not the separator either —
// "Laguna-XS-2.1" does not contain "Laguna-S-2.1", so the two files never fight.
//
// Chat template parameters (chat_template_kwargs):
//   - `enable_thinking: true/false` — binary on/off, as the S-2.1 preset also
//     documents for this family. No intermediate effort levels.
//   - NO preserve_thinking here (see above).
//
// Sampling: left UNSET, following the standing Poolside ruling that the
// checkpoint's generation_config.json is authoritative. These three ship
// temperature=1.0, top_p=1.0, min_p=0.0 (XS-2.1 adds top_k=20).
//
// Output budget note: XS.2 and M.1 declare max_new_tokens=4096 in
// generation_config.json, while XS-2.1 declares 32768. The ladder below wins for
// every request, because the extension always sends an explicit max_tokens —
// the checkpoint's 4096 default would truncate long thinking turns.
//
// To apply manually, merge "config" into an existing model entry.
// Keep that entry's id, server and actual server model ID unchanged.


{
  "presetVersion": 1,
  "match": ["Laguna-XS.2", "Laguna-M.1", "Laguna-XS-2.1"],
  "meta": {
    "source": "https://huggingface.co/poolside/Laguna-XS.2",
    "verified": "2026-11-10",
    "notes": "Poolside Laguna XS.2 / M.1 / XS-2.1 (laguna, text-only, 262K). Binary enable_thinking; unlike Laguna-S-2.1 these templates have no preserve_thinking variable, so it is not sent. Sampling left to the checkpoint as usual for Poolside."
  },
  "config": {
    "displayName": "Laguna",
    "family": "laguna",
    "maxOutputTokens": [32768, 16384, 8192],
    "capabilities": {
      "toolCalling": true,
      "imageInput": false
    },
    "modelModes": {
      "high": {
        "chat_template_kwargs": {
          "enable_thinking": true
        }
      },
      "none": {
        "chat_template_kwargs": {
          "enable_thinking": false
        }
      }
    },
    "defaultMode": "high"
  }
}
